"""dev - the Machiya dev stack: every service, synthetic data only, Hister's users as the sign-in (docs/dev-stack.md).

    ./dev init [--url URL] [--behind-serve] [--bind ADDR] [--data DIR] [--native] [--siblings DIR]
               [--tailnet-users LOGINS] [--project NAME] [--signin-provider oidc|""]
    ./dev up                 build and start everything (the vault mirror first), wait, then seed Hister once
    ./dev seed               (again) the synthetic Hister corpus: pages, labels, collections, history; idempotent
    ./dev check [--browser] [--shots DIR]   the checks (HTTP; --browser adds Playwright, Chromium and WebKit)
    ./dev status             the addresses, and what runs
    ./dev logs SERVICE       a service's log
    ./dev down               stop it (the data stays)
    ./dev reset [--yes]      down, delete the data, init with the same settings, up: the same seed again

The public base is https://localhost by default: `front` terminates TLS with a throwaway CA made here
($DEV_DATA/certs/ca.crt; the helper sends a browser back only to https addresses). On the tailnet, init with
--url https://<this machine's tailnet name> --behind-serve: Tailscale Serve terminates TLS and the front speaks http.

init writes $DEV_DATA (default: ./data here; `--data` or MACHIYA_DEV_DATA elsewhere, remembered in .data-dir): the
sample vault plus seed/vault as a bare git repository with fixed commit dates (the same commit on every machine), the
board's clone, generated secrets (0600, never printed: the dummy owner's password and Hister token, the OIDC client
secret, SearXNG's secret, the fake NewsBlur's token), the dummy owner in Hister (`hister create-user` in a pseudo-TTY),
bound to the stub OIDC provider's login, and dev.env (the compose's settings: no secrets in it).

Engines: rootless podman (`podman compose`, a user API socket is started under $DEV_DATA when DOCKER_HOST is unset),
Docker (`docker compose`), or --native: every service as a plain process from the checkouts (compose.yml's x-native
blocks; Hister from $HISTER_BIN or `hister` on PATH, SearXNG optional), for hosts without containers.
The rooms are built from checkouts of kura, niwa and konbini next to the machiya checkout (or --siblings).
Standard library only (--native also needs pyyaml, which the rooms need anyway).
"""
